  <ym-title|Same-data annulus and recording
  binding><label|same-data-annulus-and-recording-binding>

  <section|Status><label|status>

  Draft, awaiting independent mathematical and source review. Source pin:
  <verbatim|3456e5e75cf8d4cd558955a5c7638fba2d68f464> from
  <verbatim|source/upstream.json>.

  Owned prose: <verbatim|manuscript/existence/annulus-same-data-binding.tex>.

  <section|Exact selected source chain><label|exact-selected-source-chain>

  The common-response construction is <verbatim|YM.Stationary.pouring> in
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/Next/STATIONARY/FullPlanned.lean>:

  <\enumerate>
    <item><verbatim|vintageWilson> chooses one fee-bounded grey Wilson jar
    <verbatim|H>.

    <item><verbatim|saunter> chooses one correction jar <verbatim|T> for the
    supplied same path, bed, clips, and full side sequence. It gives fees,
    soft order three, and <verbatim|bindV> of the intended finite action
    minus the Wilson action at every side in that sequence.

    <item><verbatim|F := T.combine H> is the single response used thereafter.
    <verbatim|Jar.fees.pay> supplies the common strip and summed fee.
    <verbatim|Jar.sequelQ> adds the three response identities (zero-, one-,
    and two-mark layers); <verbatim|Jar.cast_book> turns them into the exact
    <verbatim|Ticket F.cast (fineFlare ...)> for each side.

    <item>The same <verbatim|F> supplies <verbatim|Play>, and the original
    same bed/path/side sequence supplies metric strip, floor, and sworn data.
    <verbatim|massifTabs> assembles these into <verbatim|HouseWord>.
    <verbatim|HouseWord.done> produces a strip-bound analytic regulated
    response and <verbatim|profit> produces <verbatim|Awards> and the full
    mesh <verbatim|Recorded> conclusion. In the <verbatim|profit> error, the
    scale factor is <verbatim|cents(m_i)> and its residual tends to zero
    along the original arbitrary sequence; no extraction is used.

    <item>The same Wilson baseline <verbatim|H> is the one used by
    <verbatim|astronomy>. The theorem is uniform over every <verbatim|Orion>
    datum built from the correction jar, and <verbatim|pouring> instantiates
    it with the exact <verbatim|T>, bed, clip, regulator and combined jar
    already used in the <verbatim|HouseWord>. Its radial bounds then feed
    <verbatim|absoluteGeode> for the log drift. This is the same
    kernel/picture which <verbatim|profit> records; the two arguments do not
    select separate response families.
  </enumerate>

  For a fixed requested odd blocking side <verbatim|L>, the regulated
  response uses <verbatim|mu=1/L>; hence its strip width and Fourier-tail
  constants may depend on <verbatim|L>. The logarithmic constants do not:
  <verbatim|astronomy> chooses the two wave constants before this
  <verbatim|L> is fixed and is quantified over every eligible
  <verbatim|Orion>. The factor convention is
  <verbatim|Y_ij(p)=1/2\<big-int\>F_ij(p,q)dq>, with mixed two-leg
  coefficient <verbatim|2Y>; the finite recorded realization is therefore
  <verbatim|side^4 * 2Y>, consistent with <verbatim|Recorded> in
  <verbatim|Pathways.lean>.

  The finite determinant identity comes from <verbatim|gemF>
  (<verbatim|OneLoop/Lattice.lean>), with <verbatim|Awards> and
  <verbatim|PoleTest> from <verbatim|Spectral/AuxReferences.lean>. The
  quadratic log-determinant formula is expanded in
  <verbatim|annulus-recording-yield.tex>, and the all-mesh Fourier alias tail
  is proved there. The local face inputs are supplied by <verbatim|getReals>,
  <verbatim|Rally.register>, <verbatim|Rally.shell>, and <verbatim|astronomy>
  in <verbatim|Lean/YM/Next/STATIONARY/OneLoop/Bubbles.lean>. In
  <verbatim|getReals>, one selected frame sequence produces both interacting
  and ghost vectors (<verbatim|Floe.vector>, <verbatim|Floe.ghost>) and their
  <verbatim|Week>/<verbatim|Tall> controls. The accepted Fleet-face chapter
  derives the actual total-field and shell-separated prices from these
  controls, the same-bed denominator identities, and the massive ghost film.
  <verbatim|astronomy> uses the all-centered population at
  <verbatim|\|x\|+mu> and the restricted shell population at <verbatim|\|x\|>
  only for <verbatim|mu\<less\>=\|x\|>.

  The call from the public stationary route is
  <verbatim|YM.Stationary.pouring> to <verbatim|YM.Stationary.Fluent>, then
  <verbatim|YM.Stationary.transition_cap> in
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/Next/STATIONARY/Level/Transition.lean>; the schedule
  consumer is <verbatim|YM.Stationary.claiming> in
  <verbatim|Level/Recurse.lean>. The record/triplet and local finite-volume
  details are expanded in the neighboring path attachment, annulus recording,
  and Fleet-face prose units. This file only joins those already-expanded
  arguments on the common response object.

  <section|Review boundary and checks><label|review-boundary-and-checks>

  <\itemize-minus>
    <item>The Fleet-face TeX/evidence snapshot was independently reviewed at
    TeX SHA-256 <verbatim|5d59da2c59faf01b6fcd9570ed00a173fd234e5ec92180a6b2ce4e1ed189fb9d>
    and evidence SHA-256 <verbatim|d1e6091e051988fb3db8b00e17cef95f2df1acc705c3c938ebf043b117364f17>.
    The accepted scope is the row prices and their use to derive the F6
    all-centered/shell inputs. This join does not modify that file.

    <item>Inspected the source declarations listed above and their immediate
    dependencies; no Lean command or build was run.

    <item>No TeX build was run.

    <item><verbatim|git diff --no-index --check /dev/null> was run on the new
    TeX and evidence files; it printed no whitespace diagnostics (exit status
    1 is expected for a differing file).

    <item><verbatim|python3 scripts/check_blueprint.py> was not rerun because
    the parent-owned <verbatim|blueprint/units/YM-000026/unit.json> remains
    absent in this clone.
  </itemize-minus>

